A||||1||wwh0001||Heater Hose||||1||
Z||000000||wwh0001||03-06-2000||12:49 PM||||On My 87 Gt the right Rear lower Heater Hose is leaking. The hose appears to be pressed into the pipe. How do you replace just the Hose? Seems like it would leak if you just cut the hose off and tried to put another one on. Other than being pressed onto the pipe it looks like a normal 5/8 heater hose ? <BR>Any ideas. Thanks.||||reg||1
Z||000001||fiero56||03-06-2000||02:38 PM||||I'll tell you what I do. I haven't had to do this on the Fiero yet, but have done it on other cars. I pull out the ol' dremel and slice the aluminum lengthwise, allowing a flat-head screwdriver to pry it open. Then take off hose and pressed clamp. Replace hose and use a regular type hose clamp.  If you do this, be careful not to scratch the metal piper underneath with the dremel bit. Just make sure it isn't a high pressure fitting for a/c or other. Good luck.<p>[This message has been edited by fiero56 (edited 03-06-2000).]||||reg||1
